+## Implemented and corrected contracts
+
+1. **Company-qualified organization and workload.** Department company_id is required; composite keys enforce same-company parents and non-null person-department company equality. Existing hierarchy depth20/cycle/invalid-parent behavior is retained. The seed rebuilds exactly50,000 T1 people,500 T2 people,2,000 T1 departments,20 seed roles and1,000,000 nonfixture learning facts with valid mixed-company organization. T2 has500 same display names/different IDs. Exact formulas/distributions/fixed IDs/fields/history groups are in `docs/task4-seed-contract.md`, derived from generator arithmetic rather than copying query output.
+2. **Strict direct team and independent project permissions.** Central makeScope maps registered team-enrollment actions to managerId=actor. M can add/remove direct A and cross-department B; C/D/E, missing, foreign, disabled/deleted and company-excluded targets deny. Team switch gates only team sources. Project appointment capabilities explicitly include add/remove and remain usable with the switch off. Batches1..200 validate every target before one mutation; mixed failures write nothing. Revision lock precedes authorization and row locks. Real wait/revoke and save-before-revoke controls pass.
+3. **Mixed-company project and company grants.** Authorized roster/count/search/progress/attachment use current person projection plus stored roster company. Shared course access uses unchanged Task3 content policy. T07 tests give X/Y legitimate same-company departments before proving customer-manager positive/negative paths; ordinary customer person-00001 is valid bulk data, has no backend roster but can browse shared published content. Internal M is a level2 non-super with own I plus only explicit company grants. Selected-source company-grant commands enforce exact delegable action, target cap/internal status, old/desired company bounds, revision and dependency invalidation. Other company grants survive revoke. Whole-project save checks all affected roster companies, including invisible members.
+4. **Minimal account.** Own wallet groups by actor/company/currency without source payload. Management list/detail/source/export stay under separate node/actions/current status/data-company predicates. Entries bind their source to the same company. A30 debt remains when B20 reward exists; same-company credit debt10 actually offsets reward10; different currency rejects. Offset validates both entries with the same action plan, same person/company/currency/kinds, then sorted row locks and an audit row. This is not the formal credit engine. `/account/export` is currently synchronous protected JSON, explicitly handed to Task5 for chunked protected output/revocation/leakage work.
+5. **Current versus history.** Manager/job null clears and state/transfer updates deliver report/training/account projections in the same marked authority transaction. History preserves immutable person/data company/department/job/status; current filters support enabled/disabled/deleted/all without rewriting snapshots. Transfer requires both company caps and a valid same-company department; X's new B SELF sees h-X-B, not h-X-A. List/detail/error field checks retain source-bound raw fields and generic no-object-detail refusals. Empty own department/subtree/specified/jurisdiction and unsupported node scopes fail closed; same-name tenant interference remains filtered.
+6. **Stable history/account delegation dimension.** Controller confirmed these existing T-15/management-account semantics: current authorization selects people and data_company caps select facts, so generated fact/entry IDs cannot be an authorization cutoff. History and management account now register `person-company-v1`, store exact canonical `[personId,dataCompanyId]` pairs (including people with no existing facts/entries), and runtime SQL/candidate matching intersects pairs per source. Exact delegation compares the same dimension. New same-company records appear without regrant; cross-company records deny. Old untagged fact/entry caps and unknown dimensions deny until explicit original-source recheck. Current source/organization/company changes still freeze; restored source/person still needs recheck. Other resource caps remain exact object IDs. Large pair-cap representation remains unmeasured.
+7. **Person/department command range fixes.** Controller static review identified that the prior person.update plan was not applied to target IDs. Actual RED confirmed C outside a B-only update cap could be changed despite only a broader report-view role; both candidates now apply the same-action target cap. Existing department move previously borrowed person.update. It now has registered department/all/organization.department.move, organization-owned exact department enumeration, and checks the entire moved subtree plus a non-null destination parent against its actual cap and company bounds. Person-only source denies; complete department cap permits; missing parent/child cap denies. This correctly registers an existing command rather than introducing new product scopes. Department SELF/ownDept remain unsupported.
